    "field": "Arctic climate science",
    "problem": "Quantifying the Arctic albedo feedback is challenging because the modifying response of clouds to sea ice loss lacks sufficient observational constraint, leading to uncertainty in climate models.",
    "method": "This study uses a synthesized dataset from CERES, CALIPSO, CloudSat, and MODIS satellites to investigate the response of clouds to sea ice retreat and quantify the moderating impact of cloud cover on the Arctic albedo feedback.",
    "task": "This paper investigates the response of Arctic cloud coverage to sea ice retreat and quantifies its dominant impact on the surface albedo feedback using space-based lidar observations from the CALIPSO satellite.",
